nxpwifiutl README
Overview
nxpwifiutl is a Linux userspace utility for interacting with the NXP Wi-Fi driver (nxpwifi) via the nl80211 netlink interface. It provides vendor-specific commands for configuring and debugging advanced features of NXP IW61x chipsets, including:

Host Sleep
Channel Switching
Antenna Configuration
EDMAC
VHT (802.11ac)
CSI (Channel State Information)
Clock Synchronization
Independent Reset
Raw Host Commands


Environment

Linux kernel: 6.6.52 or compatible
Requires nxpwifi.ko and nxpwifi_sdio.ko loaded
Interface names: mlan0, uap0


Basic Usage
nxpwifiutl <ifname> <cmd> [args...] [options]


ifname: Wireless interface name (e.g., mlan0, uap0)
cmd: One of the supported commands
args: Command-specific arguments
Global options:--dump or dump=1: Print outgoing netlink message
--no-dump or dump=0: Disable message dump (default)


Supported Commands

Command	Description
hscfg	Configure Host Sleep (conditions, GPIO, gap)
sleeppd	Configure PPS/uAPSD sleep period
hsoffload	Enable/disable Auto ARP, Ping, Wake-on-mDNS
channel_switch	Configure channel switch (oper class, channel, bandwidth)
antcfg	Configure antenna mode and SAD evaluation time
edmac_cfg	Configure Energy Detect MAC (2G/5G offsets, txq lock)
vhtcfg	Configure VHT IE (band, txrx, bw, capabilities, MCS map)
csi	Configure CSI collection (enable/disable or load config file)
clocksync	Configure GPIO TSF latch for clock synchronization
indrstcfg	Configure independent reset mode and GPIO pin
hostcmd	Send raw hostcmd from config file (e.g., edmac_ctrl, txpwrlimit)


hsoffload Command Details
# Query current hsoffload settings
nxpwifiutl <ifname> hsoffload

Enable or disable features individually:
autoarp=<0|1> : Enable/disable Auto ARP offload
autoping=<0|1> : Enable/disable Auto Ping offload
wakeonmdns=<0|1> : Enable/disable Wake-on-mDNS
Example:
nxpwifiutl mlan0 hsoffload autoarp=1 nxpwifiutl mlan0 hsoffload autoping=1 nxpwifiutl mlan0 hsoffload wakeonmdns=1
Output after query:

Auto-arp is enabled/disabled, Auto-ping is enabled/disabled, Wake-on-mDNS is enabled/disabled.

CSI Command Details
# Enable or disable CSI
nxpwifiutl <ifname> csi <0|1>
# 0 = disable CSI
# 1 = enable CSI (default or last config)

# Load CSI configuration from file
nxpwifiutl <ifname> csi <config_file> [--dump]


Config file format example (csi.conf):
[headID]
11 22 33 44

[tailID]
aa bb cc dd

[chipID]
61

[csifilter0]
00 11 22 33 44 55 08 00 01

headID, tailID: 4 bytes each
chipID: 1 byte
csifilterN: Up to 16 filters, each 9 bytes (MAC[6], pkt_type, subtype, flags)

Notes

Most commands support query mode (only <cmd>) and set mode (with arguments).
hostcmd requires a config file, e.g.:
nxpwifiutl mlan0 hostcmd txpwrlimit_cfg.conf txpwrlimit_2g_cfg_set

Build Instructions
For NXP i.MX Platform (Yocto SDK)

Source Yocto SDK environment:
source /opt/fsl-imx-xwayland/<version>/environment-setup-armv7at2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi

Compile:
$CC nxpwifiutl.c -o nxpwifiutl $(pkg-config --cflags --libs libnl-3.0 libnl-genl-3.0)

Using Provided Makefile
The source directory includes a Makefile, simply run:
make

Ensure libnl development packages are available in the SDK.
For x86/x64 PC (Native Linux)

Install dependencies:
sudo apt-get install libnl-3-dev libnl-genl-3-dev build-essential

Compile:
gcc nxpwifiutl.c -o nxpwifiutl $(pkg-config --cflags --libs libnl-3.0 libnl-genl-3.0)

Using Provided Makefile
The source directory includes a Makefile, simply run:
make

Copy the binary to target board (e.g., /usr/bin/).
